{"file":{"content":"The only unproved ingredient for general $c$ is the \\emph{carry-depth\nproperty}: every correction factor produced by a descent below depth two lies\nin the deep principal units $1+3^{c_0}\\Z/3^c$ (hence $\\equiv1\\bmod9$ for\n$c_0\\ge2$). Each correction is a ratio of $\\chi$-lifts of the same lower-level\nelement, which makes the property natural; for the first two descents it is\nproved (\\cref{prop:multrec}, corrections are powers of $\\rho=1+3^{c-1}$). The\ngeneral case is exactly the parity-twisted recursion of\n\\cref{prop:multrec}---now the \\emph{single} remaining step to the uniform gap:\ncarry depth $\\Rightarrow$ \\cref{thm:witness} for all $c$ $\\Rightarrow$\n\\cref{conj:mult} with $\\delta_0=\\sqrt3$ $\\Rightarrow$ (\\cref{thm:condunif})\n$\\sup_c\\gamma_c<1$.\n\\end{remark}\n\n\\subsection*{The missing ingredient, stated precisely}\n\nTo convert \\cref{prop:stab} into $\\sup_c\\gamma_c<1$ by the comparison route one\nmust propagate the approximate identities globally and contradict the exact\northogonality $\\sum_{a\\in\\ker\\chi_2}\\chi(a)=0$; by \\cref{cor:descentcomp} only\nthe bounded-level core of this propagation is still needed, and\n\\cref{conj:mult} is its sharpest form (the comparison graph below remains a\nuseful route to it).\n\n\\begin{definition}[Comparison graph]\\label{def:compgraph}\nFix $c$ and a branch bound $B$. The vertices are the states\n$U_{3^c}\\times\\Z/2$. There are two edge types.\n\\emph{Common-source edges}: for each state $x$ and $b,b'\\le B$ with\n$b\\equiv b'\\pmod2$, join $S_b(x)$ to $S_{b'}(x)$ (these realise\n$v\\sim4^{-j}v$ at equal parity; $b'-b$ odd joins","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","numLines":28,"startLine":1010,"totalLines":1138},"type":"text"}